NNAAMMEE
       escp2topbm - convert an ESC/P2 printer file to a PBM image


SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       eessccpp22ttooppbbmm [_p_r_i_n_t_f_i_l_e]


DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       This program is part of NNeettppbbmm(1).

       eessccpp22ttooppbbmm  reads  an  ESC/P2 printer control stream as input.  It pro‐
       duces a PBM image as output.

       eessccpp22ttooppbbmm filters the raster graphic  content  from  an  Epson  ESC/P2
       printer  control  stream and writes the image it would print as a stan‐
       dard (raw) PBM image.

       The input is from the file named by the  _p_r_i_n_t_f_i_l_e  argument,  or  from
       Standard  Input if you don't specify _p_r_i_n_t_f_i_l_e.  The output is to Stan‐
       dard Output.

       eessccpp22ttooppbbmm understands compression modes 0 (uncompressed)  and  1  (RLE
       compressed) in the Epson input stream.


OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       There  are no command line options defined specifically for eessccpp22ttooppbbmm,
       but it recognizes the options common to all programs based on libnetpbm
       (See
        Common Options ⟨index.html#commonoptions⟩ .)

       Before  Netpbm  10.72 (September 2015), the Netpbm common option --ppllaaiinn
       has no effect on eessccpp22ttooppbbmm .


HHIINNTTSS
       As eessccpp22ttooppbbmm is a simple program, created mainly to  test  ppbbmmttooeessccpp22,
       there are some restrictions:



       •      eessccpp22ttooppbbmm  looks  only at "ESC." sequences and ignores all data
              outside these Escape sequences.


       •      eessccpp22ttooppbbmm assumes that  only  one  raster  graphic  is  in  the
              printer stream.  If this isn't true, the result is garbage.


       •      eessccpp22ttooppbbmm assumes that all "ESC."  sequences use the same width
              value.  If this isn't true, the result is garbage.



